From: Benjamin Larsson <benjamin.larsson@genexis.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: mt7530-mdio: make the MCM reset optional

On the EcoNet EN751221 the second (MCM) MT7530 switch, reached over the
on-die switch's MDIO bus at address 0x1f, has no dedicated reset line
exposed in the SCU reset bindings (only EN751221_GSW_RST, which resets the
on-die switch). devm_reset_control_get() then fails and the MCM switch
never probes, so the four user LAN ports never come up.

Use devm_reset_control_get_optional() so the driver tolerates a missing
"mcm" reset and relies on the bootloader-initialised state; the reset
assert/deassert helpers are no-ops on a NULL reset_control.

Signed-off-by: Benjamin Larsson <benjamin.larsson@genexis.eu>
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530-mdio.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/mt7530-mdio.c
@@ -169,7 +169,7 @@
 	if (priv->mcm) {
 		dev_info(&mdiodev->dev, "MT7530 adapts as multi-chip module\n");

-		priv->rstc = devm_reset_control_get(&mdiodev->dev, "mcm");
+		priv->rstc = devm_reset_control_get_optional(&mdiodev->dev, "mcm");
 		if (IS_ERR(priv->rstc)) {
 			dev_err(&mdiodev->dev, "Couldn't get our reset line\n");
 			return PTR_ERR(priv->rstc);
